    "report_markdown":  "# Threat Model Report: E-Commerce Improved Test\n**Date:** 2026-02-04 21:56:46\n**Security Score:** 70/100\n**Unique Threats:** 4 (4 confirmed, 0 potential)\n---\n\n## 1. System Architecture\n\n**Components:**\n- **API** (API)\n- **Service** (Service)\n- **API Gateway** (API Gateway)\n- **WebClient** (WebClient)\n- **CDN** (CDN)\n- **Database** (Database)\n- **Identity Provider** (Identity Provider)\n- **Object Storage** (Object Storage)\n\n**Data Flows:**\n- webclient â?? api_gateway [websocket]\n- api_gateway â?? api [websocket]\n- api â?? service [websocket]\n- service â?? database [websocket]\n- database â?? object_storage [websocket]\n- api â?? object_storage [https]\n- service â?? object_storage [https]\n\n### Architecture Diagram\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    api([API])\n    service[Service]\n    api_gateway[API Gateway]\n    webclient{{WebClient}}\n    cdn[CDN]\n    database[(Database)]\n    identity_provider[Identity Provider]\n    object_storage[Object Storage]\n    api -- websocket --\u003e service\n    api -- https --\u003e object_storage\n    service -- websocket --\u003e database\n    service -- https --\u003e object_storage\n    api_gateway -- websocket --\u003e api\n    webclient -- websocket --\u003e api_gateway\n    database -- websocket --\u003e object_storage\n```\n\n## 2. Confirmed Risks\nThe following 4 risks are backed by verified evidence:\n\n### [CRITICAL] JWT Signature Validation Bypass\n**ID:** S-003 | **Category:** Spoofing | **Confidence:** High\n\n**Why this exists:** JWT authentication is used but signature validation is disabled or incomplete, allowing token forgery and privilege escalation.\n\n**Affected Components:** api, api_gateway\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Verified \u0027auth_type\u0027 is \u0027jwt\u0027 (Matched condition: contains jwt)\n- Verified \u0027jwt_validation\u0027 is \u0027False\u0027 (Matched condition: == False)\n\n**Mitigation:** Enable JWT signature validation on all services using a shared secret or public key infrastructure.\n\n### [MEDIUM] Unrestricted Public Access to Storage\n**ID:** ID-006 | **Category:** Information Disclosure | **Confidence:** High\n\n**Why this exists:** Storage resources are publicly accessible without signed URLs or access controls, allowing unauthorized enumeration and data scraping.\n\n**Affected Components:** cdn, object_storage\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Verified \u0027public_access\u0027 is \u0027True\u0027 (Matched condition: == True)\n- Verified \u0027signed_urls\u0027 is \u0027False\u0027 (Matched condition: != True)\n\n**Mitigation:** Implement signed URLs with time-based expiration for all storage access.\n\n### [HIGH] Unencrypted Data at Rest\n**ID:** I-001 | **Category:** Information Disclosure | **Confidence:** High\n\n**Why this exists:** The data store does not use encryption at rest, exposing data to physical theft or disk inspection.\n\n**Affected Components:** database\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Verified \u0027encryption_at_rest\u0027 is \u0027False\u0027 (Matched condition: == False)\n\n**Mitigation:** Enable Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) or server-side encryption.\n\n### [HIGH] Potential Lateral Movement (Missing Internal Auth) (Elevation of Privilege)\n**ID:** LAT-001 | **Category:** Lateral Movement | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n**Why this exists:** Internal traffic between components appears to lack authentication. If one service is compromised, attackers could move laterally to others without restriction.\n\n**Affected Data Flows:** api â?? service, api â?? object_storage, service â?? database, service â?? object_storage, api_gateway â?? api, database â?? object_storage\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Verified \u0027trust_boundary\u0027 is \u0027internal\u0027 (Matched condition: == internal)\n- Field \u0027authenticated\u0027 is not defined (no positive signal).\n\n**Mitigation:** Implement Service-to-Service authentication using mTLS or OIDC tokens.\n\n## 3. Potential Risks (Assumption-Based)\n*No potential risks detected.*\n\n\n---\n\n*Generated by AI Threat Modeler*",
